      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/satanopera_acuticeps_en/",
      "html": "<p>Brazil: Rio Branco, Negro, Solimões.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/satanopera_acuticeps_en/",
      "html": "<p>Normally the durable care of Satanopera acuticeps is only possible in soft and sour pH-value. But as it was finally successful to breed this eartheater inside the aquarium, it could be that the bred ones are easier to keep and even easier to breed. So far the breeding was possible furthermore only in soft (&lt; 4 °dGH) and sour (pH 5.5-6.0) waters at 30°C. But as the bred ones can be unproblematically raised in hard and alkaline water, it is safe to assume that their care is not as critical anymore. Of course it would be better to use soft and sour water for their care.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/satanopera_acuticeps_en/",
      "html": "<p>S. acuticeps is a cichlid which must be fed often (at least 3 times a day) and with variety.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/satanopera_acuticeps_en/",
      "html": "<p>Keeping it with greedy or aggressive fish should be avoided, because S. acuticeps can only slightly assert itself despite its size (20 cm).</p>"
    }
  ],
